"""
ONLY 5 ATOMS EVER — and relativity melts it: oganesson, element 118 (Blender 4.2+ / 5.x)   @AlexCarten_

118 electrons in 7 shells. Inner electrons move at about Z*alpha = 118/137 = 86% of light speed (gamma ~ 2).
Relativistic calculations (Jerabek et al., PRL 2018) show its shell structure smeared out almost into an electron gas;
Smits et al. (2020) predict it is a solid at room temperature (melts ~52 C), not a noble gas.
About 5 atoms made (Dubna, 2002-2005), each lasting under 1 ms.

Look: dense streak-grains flowing around the axis (orange one way, blue the other, white slow), cone cut-away,
lit with shadows, motion blur + depth of field. Shells: illustrative radial shapes.

File > New > General -> Scripting -> Open -> Run Script -> Ctrl+F12
Video: ~/OrbitalRenders/oganesson/oganesson.mp4   (music: oganesson_music.wav, same timing — drop it in CapCut at 0)
No Python runs during playback/render (baked keyframes + geometry nodes).
"""
